{"concept_id": "drv.interaction.overtake_pass_on_right", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user a overtakes and passes road user b on b's right: a overtakes and passes b from the rear, as drv.interaction.overtake_pass states it with the same window and the same heading tolerance, and makes the passage with b on its left. b is on a's left where the lateral component of b's bearing in a's frame (rel.bearing) is positive; the two are side by side where their projections on a's heading share length (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero). The act begins at the last observation of the window behind at which b was ahead of a with their headings aligned within same_dir_cos. The act is recognized at the observation at which drv.interaction.overtake_pass holds for a and b, where b is on a's left there and at every observation since the act began at which the two are side by side. The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until b has again been ahead of a and then comes to be behind it. Conduct before the window behind is not read: a pass that takes longer than the window is not recognized. It denotes the relative motion of the two road users and the side on which a passes only: it says nothing of the lanes or the pavement a uses, of whether b moves, or of why a passes. Not denoted: a pass with b on a's right at the recognition or at some observation at which the two are side by side, which is a pass on b's left; a drawing alongside b that does not clear b; b ahead of a only while their headings are not aligned. Where b's bearing or the overlap of the two bodies is unobserved at an observation the passage reads, it is unknown.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "a", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "b", "sort": "track"}], "params": [{"name": "window", "unit": "s", "meaning": "the longest duration of the pass, from having b ahead to having it behind; conduct before the window is not read"}, {"name": "same_dir_cos", "unit": "ratio", "meaning": "cosine of the largest heading difference at which a and b count as travelling in the same direction"}], "act": {"boundary": "window", "window": "window", "onset": "The act begins at the last observation of the window behind at which b was ahead of a with their headings aligned within same_dir_cos.", "recognition": "The act is recognized at the observation at which drv.interaction.overtake_pass holds for a and b, where b is on a's left there and at every observation since the act began at which the two are side by side.", "extent": "The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until b has again been ahead of a and then comes to be behind it.", "history": "Conduct before the window behind is not read: a pass that takes longer than the window is not recognized."}, "elements": [{"span": "a overtakes and passes b from the rear, as drv.interaction.overtake_pass states it with the same window and the same heading tolerance", "atoms": [], "concepts": ["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"], "justification": "The pass from the rear, its beginning, its recognition and its extent are those of drv.interaction.overtake_pass, whose contract denotes 'Road user a overtakes and passes road user b from the rear: a, travelling in the same direction as b, comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it'; this concept adds only the side, so it calls that concept with its own window and same_dir_cos rather than rebuilding it."}, {"span": "b is on a's left where the lateral component of b's bearing in a's frame (rel.bearing) is positive", "atoms": ["rel.bearing"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.bearing is the 'direction of b from a in a's frame (for \"on the right of\", \"immediately to the rear\")': its lateral component tells on which side of a the other road user lies, which is the side of the passage."}, {"span": "the two are side by side where their projections on a's heading share length (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero)", "atoms": ["rel.longitudinal_overlap"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.longitudinal_overlap: 'the bodies overlap along the subject's heading (side by side): the length the two footprints' projections on that axis share'; its exclusion (neither a contact nor a distance between the bodies) does not apply, since only the side-by-side phase of the pass is read with it."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "a follows b in the same lane with headings aligned (rel.same_direction), b ahead with no longitudinal overlap; a moves to the right, draws alongside with b's bearing lateral component positive (b on a's left) while rel.longitudinal_overlap is non-negative, and comes to have b behind it with b still on its left, all within the window: the concept holds at the observation at which b first is behind a."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The same pass made with a moving to the left: while side by side, b's bearing lateral component is negative (b on a's right), and at recognition b is behind a on its right: drv.interaction.overtake_pass holds but the passage is on b's left, so the concept does not hold."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The pass of the holds scenario with rel.bearing not observed on the source: neither the order nor the side can be read.", "masked": ["rel.bearing"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_210_1", "NRS_484B_210_2", "NRS_484B_210_3"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.lane.heading_left_of_carrier", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user a, moving, points to the left of the designated direction of travel of carrier region r by more than a tolerance: its heading has turned off r's direction toward the left. With h a's heading (kin.heading) and d r's designated direction (st.lane_direction), both as a formula reads them normalised, the dot product of d and h is positive, so that a points along d rather than against it, and the cross product d_x times h_y minus d_y times h_x exceeds sin_tol, so that h lies to the left of d, counter-clockwise in the world frame, by more than the angle whose sine is sin_tol; and a's speed (kin.speed) is above speed_tol. It is a state at one observation: it says nothing of whether a occupies r, of how long its heading has been so, of the path a will follow, or of why it turns. Not denoted: a road user at rest or moving at or below speed_tol; a heading within that angle of d, or turned to its right; a heading that points against d, the dot product being at or below zero. Where r carries no designated direction, or a's heading or speed is unobserved, it is unknown.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "a", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "r", "sort": "region"}], "params": [{"name": "sin_tol", "unit": "ratio", "meaning": "sine of the largest angle between a's heading and r's designated direction at which a counts as keeping to that direction: the heading noise and wander the observer tolerates"}, {"name": "speed_tol", "unit": "m/s", "meaning": "the speed at or below which a counts as not moving: the source's speed resolution"}], "elements": [{"span": "h a's heading (kin.heading)", "atoms": ["kin.heading"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.heading is the 'direction the body points', read normalised; the departure is of the body's pointing from the carrier's direction, not of a path."}, {"span": "d r's designated direction (st.lane_direction)", "atoms": ["st.lane_direction"], "concepts": [], "justification": "st.lane_direction is the 'direction of travel designated for a structure a vehicle travels in', local to its carrier and unknown where none is carried, which is the reference the heading departs from."}, {"span": "a's speed (kin.speed) is above speed_tol", "atoms": ["kin.speed"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.speed is the 'magnitude of velocity'; a road user at rest changes no course, so the state is read only while a moves above the tolerance."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "a moves well above speed_tol in lane r whose designated direction points east; a's heading points east-north-east, turned counter-clockwise from r's direction by clearly more than the angle whose sine is sin_tol: the concept holds."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "a moves in r with its heading aligned with r's designated direction (cross product below sin_tol): the concept does not hold."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "a moves turned to the left of the lane, but the source does not observe st.lane_direction for r.", "masked": ["st.lane_direction"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_413_2"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.lane.heading_right_of_carrier", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user a, moving, points to the right of the designated direction of travel of carrier region r by more than a tolerance: its heading has turned off r's direction toward the right. With h a's heading (kin.heading) and d r's designated direction (st.lane_direction), both as a formula reads them normalised, the dot product of d and h is positive, so that a points along d rather than against it, and the cross product d_x times h_y minus d_y times h_x is below minus sin_tol, so that h lies to the right of d, clockwise in the world frame, by more than the angle whose sine is sin_tol; and a's speed (kin.speed) is above speed_tol. It is a state at one observation: it says nothing of whether a occupies r, of how long its heading has been so, of the path a will follow, or of why it turns. Not denoted: a road user at rest or moving at or below speed_tol; a heading within that angle of d, or turned to its left; a heading that points against d, the dot product being at or below zero. Where r carries no designated direction, or a's heading or speed is unobserved, it is unknown.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "a", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "r", "sort": "region"}], "params": [{"name": "sin_tol", "unit": "ratio", "meaning": "sine of the largest angle between a's heading and r's designated direction at which a counts as keeping to that direction: the heading noise and wander the observer tolerates"}, {"name": "speed_tol", "unit": "m/s", "meaning": "the speed at or below which a counts as not moving: the source's speed resolution"}], "elements": [{"span": "h a's heading (kin.heading)", "atoms": ["kin.heading"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.heading is the 'direction the body points', read normalised; the departure is of the body's pointing from the carrier's direction, not of a path."}, {"span": "d r's designated direction (st.lane_direction)", "atoms": ["st.lane_direction"], "concepts": [], "justification": "st.lane_direction is the 'direction of travel designated for a structure a vehicle travels in', local to its carrier and unknown where none is carried, which is the reference the heading departs from."}, {"span": "a's speed (kin.speed) is above speed_tol", "atoms": ["kin.speed"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.speed is the 'magnitude of velocity'; a road user at rest changes no course, so the state is read only while a moves above the tolerance."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "a moves well above speed_tol in lane r whose designated direction points east; a's heading points east-south-east, turned clockwise from r's direction by clearly more than the angle whose sine is sin_tol: the concept holds."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "a moves in r with its heading aligned with r's designated direction (cross product above minus sin_tol): the concept does not hold."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "a moves turned to the right of the lane, but the source does not observe st.lane_direction for r.", "masked": ["st.lane_direction"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_413_2"], "supersedes": null}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_210_1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-210-1"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "may overtake and pass upon the right of another vehicle only under the following conditions:", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "(a) When the driver of the vehicle overtaken is making or signaling to make a left turn.", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "(b) Upon a highway with unobstructed pavement which is not occupied by parked vehicles and which is of sufficient width for two or more lines of moving vehicles in each direction.", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "(c) Upon a highway with unobstructed pavement which is not marked as a traffic lane and which is not occupied by parked vehicles,", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "if the vehicle that is overtaking and passing another vehicle:", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "(1) Except as otherwise provided in subsection 4 [(4) appended below],", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "does not travel more than 200 feet in the section of pavement not marked as a traffic lane;", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "or (2) While being driven in the section of pavement not marked as a traffic lane, does not travel through an intersection", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s10", "text": "or past any private way that is used to enter or exit the highway.", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s11", "text": "(d) Upon any highway on which traffic is restricted to one direction of movement, where the highway is free from obstructions and of sufficient width for two or more lines of moving vehicles.", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s12", "text": "The provisions of subparagraph (1) of paragraph (c) of subsection 1 do not apply to: (a) An authorized emergency vehicle", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s13", "text": "described in NRS 484A.480;", "role": "reference"}, {"id": "s14", "text": "(b) A vehicle which has been issued a permit to operate as an authorized emergency vehicle", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s15", "text": "pursuant to NRS 484A.490;", "role": "reference"}, {"id": "s16", "text": "(c) A traffic incident management vehicle;", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s17", "text": "(d) A tow car;", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s18", "text": "(e) A coroner vehicle;", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s19", "text": "or (f) A public transit motor bus,", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s20", "text": "that is being driven on the paved shoulder of a highway", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s21", "text": "where lawfully placed signage allows that vehicle to use the shoulder in that manner.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate'), claimed whole, never expanded into classes. 'driver' (DEF-NRS-484A-080, 'every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle') is a relational role, not membership: it is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading, agency)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.overtake_pass_on_right"], "justification": "'overtake and pass upon the right of another vehicle' is the act drv.interaction.overtake_pass_on_right(subject, b), whose contract denotes 'Road user a overtakes and passes road user b on b's right'; the other vehicle b is of the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle. 'only under the following conditions' forbids the act unless one of the listed conditions holds, so each condition is an exception to the prohibition."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["sig.turn_indicator", "sig.hand_signal"], "derived": ["drv.motion.left_turn"], "justification": "The vehicle overtaken is b. 'signaling to make a left turn' is the signal itself, not a declared intention: sig.turn_indicator 'the turn indicator state in {off, left, right}' at left, or sig.hand_signal 'a driver's or rider's arm signal' of meaning left; the indicator's exclusion (not the turn itself) does not apply, since the words name the signal. 'is making ... a left turn' is b's act drv.motion.left_turn, 'Road user a has completed a turn to the left', read as recognized within its window ahead of the observation, so that a turn under way is caught by its completion (narrowing). 'the driver of' is read through b's controlled motion (agency)."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.highway", "st.on_way", "st.obstruction", "st.roadway", "st.lane", "st.lane_adjacency", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.parked"], "justification": "'Upon a highway': the subject's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) an st.highway, 'the entire public way between its boundary lines'. 'unobstructed pavement': no st.obstruction ('a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user') lies on that way (st.on_way). 'not occupied by parked vehicles': no road user of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle that is drv.motion.parked ('the standing of a vehicle, whether occupied or not') occupies a roadway (st.roadway) the subject occupies. 'sufficient width for two or more lines of moving vehicles in each direction': an st.lane is 'a longitudinal strip of roadway for one line of vehicles', so width for two lines in a direction is a count of lanes in that direction (st.lane_adjacency 'the count of lanes in that direction') of at least the stated two, for every lane lying on the highway (each direction)."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.highway", "st.on_way", "st.obstruction", "st.shoulder", "st.roadway", "st.lane", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.parked"], "justification": "'pavement which is not marked as a traffic lane': the subject occupies an st.shoulder whose paved attribute is set ('the part of the highway beside the roadway ...; paved attribute'), or occupies an st.roadway while occupying no st.lane; 'unobstructed' and 'not occupied by parked vehicles' as in s4, read on the highway (st.on_way) and on the shoulder or roadway section the subject occupies (rel.occupies)."}, {"span": "s8", "atoms": ["kin.path_length", "rel.occupies", "st.shoulder", "st.roadway", "st.lane"], "derived": [], "justification": "'does not travel more than 200 feet in the section of pavement not marked as a traffic lane': the distance the subject has travelled (kin.path_length, 'distance travelled along the body's path') while continuously occupying that section (a paved st.shoulder, or an st.roadway outside every st.lane), read with Term.distanceWhile at the recognition of the pass, is at most the stated 200 feet."}, {"span": "s9", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "st.shoulder", "st.roadway", "st.lane"], "derived": [], "justification": "'While being driven in the section of pavement not marked as a traffic lane, does not travel through an intersection': since the subject came onto that section and while it stays on it, its footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) no st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet'; an alley junction is no st.intersection by that contract, as DEF-NRS-484A-105 (3) excludes it. 'being driven' is read through controlled motion (agency)."}, {"span": "s10", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.driveway_or_alley_entrance"], "derived": [], "justification": "Nearest atoms only: 'past any private way that is used to enter or exit the highway' would be read as the subject's footprint overlapping the entrance of a private way while on the section. st.driveway_or_alley_entrance is 'private road, alley or driveway meeting the highway' and its contract states 'Not a stand-in for: which of them meets the highway there — the kind does not tell an alley's entrance from a private road's or driveway's'; a private way (DEF-NRS-484A-190, 'every way or place in private ownership') excludes an alley, which is a highway. The span is a gap."}, {"span": "s11", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.one_way_roadway", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic", "st.highway", "st.on_way", "st.obstruction", "st.lane", "st.lane_adjacency"], "derived": [], "justification": "'any highway on which traffic is restricted to one direction of movement': the subject occupies an st.one_way_roadway, 'roadway on which traffic is restricted to one direction' — the restriction binds the road users of DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, the aggregate the contract's 'traffic' carries. 'free from obstructions': no st.obstruction lies on the highway (st.on_way). 'sufficient width for two or more lines of moving vehicles': every lane on that highway has a lane count in its direction (st.lane_adjacency) of at least the stated two."}, {"span": "s12", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'do not apply to ... An authorized emergency vehicle': the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle ('a vehicle permitted to depart from certain traffic laws'), never expanded; for its members the 200-foot limit of (c)(1) is met."}, {"span": "s14", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'A vehicle which has been issued a permit to operate as an authorized emergency vehicle': the permit is a legal status whose evidence is the vehicle's membership of DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle, 'a vehicle permitted to depart from certain traffic laws' (observable_reading, status)."}, {"span": "s16", "atoms": ["ru.official_vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'A traffic incident management vehicle': ru.official_vehicle 'a vehicle in official or contracted road service' of kind incident_management; its exclusion (not an emergency vehicle) agrees with the words."}, {"span": "s17", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-280::tow_car"], "derived": [], "justification": "'A tow car' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-280::tow_car, claimed whole."}, {"span": "s18", "atoms": ["ru.official_vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'A coroner vehicle': ru.official_vehicle of kind coroner."}, {"span": "s19", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus", "ru.transit_bus"], "derived": [], "justification": "'bus' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus; the law's own qualifier 'public transit' limits its members to ru.transit_bus, 'bus in public transit service, identifiable by its livery or route display', leaving out school, private and charter buses."}, {"span": "s20", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.shoulder", "st.highway", "st.on_way"], "derived": [], "justification": "'being driven on the paved shoulder of a highway': the exempt vehicle's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) an st.shoulder whose paved attribute is set, lying on the highway (st.on_way); 'being driven' is read through controlled motion (agency)."}, {"span": "s21", "atoms": ["dev.regulatory_sign", "dev.governs", "prim.conditions_hold"], "derived": [], "justification": "'lawfully placed signage allows that vehicle to use the shoulder': a dev.regulatory_sign of code shoulder_use_permitted that governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls — ... or shoulder') the shoulder occupied, whose conditions hold for the subject (prim.conditions_hold: 'any occupancy or class condition is met'); 'lawfully placed' is read through the sign's presence (observable_reading, status); the sign is not a stand-in for a manoeuvre, being read as a condition."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "s7", "why": "The words point to subsection 4, whose exemption is carried by spans s12 to s21; they add no restriction of their own: the duty is the same whether or not they are read.", "scope": "none"}, {"span": "s13", "why": "NRS 484A.480 is not a law of this corpus; the class it describes is carried by the aggregate on s12."}, {"span": "s15", "why": "NRS 484A.490 is not a law of this corpus; the permitted class is carried by the aggregate on s14."}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject, of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, overtakes and passes on its right another road user b of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle: drv.interaction.overtake_pass_on_right(subject, b) with p.overtake_window and p.overtake_same_direction_cos is recognized at the judged observation. b is quantified there, not a binder.", "obligation": "At that recognition at least one of the following holds; otherwise the duty is violated. (a) At every observation of the act, b shows sig.turn_indicator left or sig.hand_signal left, or drv.motion.left_turn(b) with p.turn_window, p.turn_heading_min, p.u_turn_heading_min and p.turn_yaw_rate_tol holds within p.turn_window ahead of that observation. (b) At every observation of the act, the subject occupies a highway h on which no st.obstruction lies (st.on_way), no road user of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle that is drv.motion.parked (p.halt_speed_tolerance, p.parking_min_duration) occupies a roadway the subject occupies, and every lane lying on h has, in its direction, an st.lane_adjacency count of at least the stated two. (c) At every observation of the act, the subject occupies a highway h on which no obstruction lies, and occupies pavement not marked as a lane (a paved st.shoulder, or an st.roadway while occupying no st.lane) that no parked vehicle of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle occupies; and, at recognition, either (c1) the path length travelled while continuously on that pavement (Term.distanceWhile) is at most the stated 200 feet, or the subject is exempt under subsection 4, or (c2) since it came onto that pavement it has occupied no st.intersection and no private-way entrance (the gap of span s10). Exempt under subsection 4: the subject is of DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle, of DEF-NRS-484A-280::tow_car, an ru.official_vehicle of kind incident_management or coroner, or of DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus and ru.transit_bus, and at every observation of the act it occupies a paved st.shoulder lying on the highway that a dev.regulatory_sign of code shoulder_use_permitted governs (dev.governs) with prim.conditions_hold for the subject. (d) At every observation of the act, the subject occupies an st.one_way_roadway on a highway on which no obstruction lies and every lane lying on that highway has an st.lane_adjacency count in its direction of at least the stated two.", "params": ["p.overtake_window", "p.overtake_same_direction_cos", "p.turn_window", "p.turn_heading_min", "p.u_turn_heading_min", "p.turn_yaw_rate_tol", "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.parking_min_duration"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'The driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "'is making ... a left turn' is read by the completion of b's left turn within the turn window ahead of the observation; a turn completed later than the window is not read, and a turn begun just after the observation counts.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "'unobstructed pavement' is read as no obstruction lying on the highway the subject occupies, including objects beside the roadway that the source records on that way.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s8", "why": "The distance travelled on the unmarked pavement is read at the recognition of the pass, accumulated since the subject came onto that pavement; travel on it after the recognition is not read.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s14", "why": "The permit is a legal status read through the vehicle's membership of the authorized-emergency-vehicle aggregate.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s21", "why": "'lawfully placed signage' is read through the presence of the shoulder-use sign governing the shoulder.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "On a two-way highway whose every lane has an st.lane_adjacency count of one in its direction, the subject follows b in the same lane, moves right within the roadway and lanes, and passes b with b on its left; b shows sig.turn_indicator off and sig.hand_signal no_signal and makes no left turn; the subject never occupies a shoulder: no condition holds."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "b is halted with sig.turn_indicator left at every observation of the act; the subject passes it on its right within the roadway: condition (a) holds."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject travels alone on the highway, no road user ahead of it; no pass is recognized."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The subject draws past b as in forbid but the source does not observe rel.bearing: whether a pass on the right occurred is unknown.", "masked": ["rel.bearing"]}, {"name": "occasion_s3", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "As forbid, but b shows sig.turn_indicator left only during the first part of the act and off afterwards, and makes no left turn: (a) holds for part of the act only."}, {"name": "occasion_s3_outside", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but b shows sig.turn_indicator left at every observation of the act, having shown off before the act began."}, {"name": "occasion_s4", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The pass begins on a highway whose lanes count two in each direction and ends after a lane drop to one lane in each direction; b gives no signal: (b) holds for part of the act only."}, {"name": "occasion_s4_outside", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The h