ange heading angles in naturalistic driving data"}, {"name": "p.conflict_horizon", "unit": "s", "value": 3.0, "convention": "time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash", "source": "traffic-conflict technique; FHWA Surrogate Safety Assessment Model"}, {"name": "p.conflict_centre_clearance", "unit": "m", "value": 3.0, "convention": "centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width", "source": "AASHTO passenger-car design-vehicle dimensions"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
