 road user', being negative: the centre line lies to the right of the subject's reference point. 'driven' is read through controlled motion (agency)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.lane", "st.lane_adjacency", "st.on_way", "st.highway", "st.centre_line", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'two-directional highway' (DEF-NRS-484B-073) is 'an undivided highway upon which vehicles are allowed to proceed in opposite directions': the highway the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.highway) carries an st.centre_line, which divides 'the two directions of a two-way roadway', one roadway, so the way is undivided. 'two-lane': every st.lane lying on that highway (st.on_way) has an st.lane_adjacency 'count of the lanes in that direction' of a single lane, so the two directions carry the stated two lanes; the lane contract's exclusion ('lane ordinal equals roadway half only on a two-lane road') is met, the road being two-lane."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"], "justification": "'overtaking and passing another vehicle proceeding in the same direction' is drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, b): 'a, travelling in the same direction as b, comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it'; b is of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["st.sight_distance"], "derived": [], "justification": "'such left side is clearly visible': st.sight_distance at the subject's point, 'the distance along the road within which a vehicle at a point and another vehicle on the road could see each other ... whether or not any road user is there'; what a driver could see is read through that place's sight distance (observable_reading, perception), not rel.visible, since no actual road user need be there. Its extent is bounded by the standard of s7."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic", "rel.oncoming", "rel.centre_distance"], "derived": [], "justification": "