c driving data"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_213_1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-213-1"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "A vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "must not be driven to the left side of the center", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "of a two-lane, two-directional highway", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "and overtaking and passing another vehicle proceeding in the same direction,", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "unless such left side is clearly visible", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "and is free of oncoming traffic", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "for a sufficient distance ahead to permit such overtaking and passing to be completely made without interfering with the safe operation of any vehicle approaching from the opposite direction or any vehicle overtaken.", "role": "standard"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'A vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate'), claimed whole."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["prim.region_lateral_offset", "st.centre_line", "st.on_way", "st.highway", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'center' (DEF-NRS-484A-040) is 'a continuous or broken line marked upon the surface of a highway ... to indicate each portion of a highway allocated to traffic proceeding in the two opposite directions, and, if a line is not marked, it is an imaginary line in the highway equally distant from the edges or curbs': st.centre_line, 'the marking, or the geometric centre, dividing the two directions of a two-way roadway', lying (st.on_way) on the st.highway the subject occupies (rel.occupies). 'to the left side of the center' is prim.region_lateral_offset(subject, c), 'the signed lateral offset (m, left positive) of a structure region from a