c driving data"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_213_1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-213-1"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "A vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "must not be driven to the left side of the center", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "of a two-lane, two-directional highway", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "and overtaking and passing another vehicle proceeding in the same direction,", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "unless such left side is clearly visible", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "and is free of oncoming traffic", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "for a sufficient distance ahead to permit such overtaking and passing to be completely made without interfering with the safe operation of any vehicle approaching from the opposite direction or any vehicle overtaken.", "role": "standard"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'A vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate'), claimed whole."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["prim.region_lateral_offset", "st.centre_line", "st.on_way", "st.highway", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'center' (DEF-NRS-484A-040) is 'a continuous or broken line marked upon the surface of a highway ... to indicate each portion of a highway allocated to traffic proceeding in the two opposite directions, and, if a line is not marked, it is an imaginary line in the highway equally distant from the edges or curbs': st.centre_line, 'the marking, or the geometric centre, dividing the two directions of a two-way roadway', lying (st.on_way) on the st.highway the subject occupies (rel.occupies). 'to the left side of the center' is prim.region_lateral_offset(subject, c), 'the signed lateral offset (m, left positive) of a structure region from a road user', being negative: the centre line lies to the right of the subject's reference point. 'driven' is read through controlled motion (agency)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.lane", "st.lane_adjacency", "st.on_way", "st.highway", "st.centre_line", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'two-directional highway' (DEF-NRS-484B-073) is 'an undivided highway upon which vehicles are allowed to proceed in opposite directions': the highway the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.highway) carries an st.centre_line, which divides 'the two directions of a two-way roadway', one roadway, so the way is undivided. 'two-lane': every st.lane lying on that highway (st.on_way) has an st.lane_adjacency 'count of the lanes in that direction' of a single lane, so the two directions carry the stated two lanes; the lane contract's exclusion ('lane ordinal equals roadway half only on a two-lane road') is met, the road being two-lane."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"], "justification": "'overtaking and passing another vehicle proceeding in the same direction' is drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, b): 'a, travelling in the same direction as b, comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it'; b is of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["st.sight_distance"], "derived": [], "justification": "'such left side is clearly visible': st.sight_distance at the subject's point, 'the distance along the road within which a vehicle at a point and another vehicle on the road could see each other ... whether or not any road user is there'; what a driver could see is read through that place's sight distance (observable_reading, perception), not rel.visible, since no actual road user need be there. Its extent is bounded by the standard of s7."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic", "rel.oncoming", "rel.centre_distance"], "derived": [], "justification": "