"span": "s2", "why": "'driven' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "'the driver's view' is read through the sight distance of the subject's place, what could be seen from it, not through any driver's perception.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "perception"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The subject moves toward an st.crest whose ground distance is below its speed times p.passing_sight_time; st.sight_distance at its point is below that distance; its reference point lies left of the centre line of the highway it occupies."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same approach to the crest with the subject right of the centre line (prim.region_lateral_offset to the line positive)."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "On a straight, level two-way highway (curvature at resolution, no crest ahead, sight distance far above the bound), the subject drives left of the centre line."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The subject is left of the centre line approaching a crest; st.sight_distance is not observed.", "masked": ["st.sight_distance"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "On a curve (st.curvature above p.curvature_resolution) with st.sight_distance below the subject's speed times p.passing_sight_time and no crest, the subject is left of the centre line."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject approaches a crest with short sight distance on an st.one_way_roadway, left of the roadway's geometric centre."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.passing_sight_time", "unit": "s", "value": 11.0, "convention": "the MUTCD minimum passing sight distance (Table 3B-1, the warrant for a no-passing zone) divided by the prevailing speed it is tabulated for: about eleven seconds of travel across 25 to 70 mph; the sight distance or the clear distance a pass needs is the subject's speed times this time", "source": "MUTCD 2009 Section 3B.02, Table 3B-1"}, {"name": "p.curvature_resolution", "unit": "1/m", "value": 0.0005, "convention": "the horizontal curvature at or below which a mapped roadway reads as straight: the curvature resolution of map centrelines (a radius of about two kilometres)", "source": "map centreline curvature resolution of the acquisition source"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
