_centre_clearance."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The subject passes b on b's right in the adjacent lane keeping its distance; no closest approach within p.conflict_horizon falls below p.conflict_centre_clearance and no contact occurs; no other road user is in the scene."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject follows b in the same lane at a steady gap and never passes it."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The subject draws past b on its right but rel.bearing is not observed: whether a pass on the right occurred is unknown.", "masked": ["rel.bearing"]}], "occasion": {"act": "drv.interaction.overtake_pass_on_right", "boundary": "window", "window": "p.overtake_window", "under_way": {"words": "overtake and pass another vehicle upon the right", "atoms": ["kin.velocity", "rel.bearing", "rel.longitudinal_overlap", "rel.same_direction"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.overtake_pass_on_right"], "justification": "An observation inside the act lies after its beginning, the last observation of the window behind at which b was ahead of the subject with headings aligned (rel.bearing longitudinal component positive, rel.longitudinal_overlap negative, rel.same_direction), and at or before its recognition. These relations are computed from the two road users' kinematics, so the boundary reads their relative motion, never a place."}, "spans": {}}, "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.overtake_window", "unit": "s", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the longest duration of an overtaking manoeuvre on an urban street, from having the overtaken vehicle ahead to having it behind", "source": "overtaking-manoeuvre durations in naturalistic driving studies"}, {"name": "p.overtake_same_direction_cos", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.9, "convention": "cosine of the largest heading difference (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as travelling in the same direction while one moves out to pass the