rection_cos is recognized at the judged observation; and at some observation of the act (from its beginning, the last observation of the window behind at which b was ahead with aligned headings, to its recognition) the subject occupies a highway h on which an st.centre_line c lies and every lane lying on h has a single lane in its direction (st.lane_adjacency count), the two-lane two-directional highway. b is quantified there, not a binder.", "obligation": "At every observation of the act at which the subject occupies such a highway h and prim.region_lateral_offset(subject, c) is negative for a centre line c lying on h (the subject on the left side of the center), all of the following hold; otherwise the duty is violated: st.sight_distance at the subject's point is at least the subject's kin.speed times p.passing_sight_time; every road user u of DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic with rel.oncoming(subject, u) under p.oncoming_heading_cos is at a rel.centre_distance of at least that same distance; and neither b nor any road user u of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle oncoming to the subject is in rel.contact with the subject, or has prim.closest_approach_within(subject, u) over p.conflict_horizon with prim.closest_approach_distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance.", "params": ["p.overtake_window", "p.overtake_same_direction_cos", "p.passing_sight_time", "p.oncoming_heading_cos", "p.conflict_horizon", "p.conflict_centre_clearance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s2", "why": "'driven to the left side of the center' is read as the subject's reference point lying beyond the centre line to its left; a body that only straddles the line with its reference point on the right is not read.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "'driven' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "'clearly visible' is read through the sight distance of the subject's place, what could be seen from it, not through any driver's perception.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "perception"}, {"span": "s7", "why": "The exception is read at the observations of the act at which the subject is on the left side of the center: visibility and freedom from oncoming traffic are required while the left side is used.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "On a highway with a centre line and one lane in each direction, the subject moves left of the centre line to pass b; a road user u of traffic is oncoming in that lane at a centre distance below the subject's speed times p.passing_sight_time, and its closest approach within p.conflict_horizon falls below p.conflict_centre_clearance; the pass is recognized."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same pass with st.sight_distance at the subject's point far above its speed times p.passing_sight_time at every observation of the act and no oncoming road user in the scene; the subject keeps clear of b."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject follows b on the two-lane highway without passing it."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The pass of permit with st.sight_distance not observed on the source.", "masked": ["st.sight_distance"]}, {"name": "occasion_s3", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The pass begins where the highway has two lanes in each direction and, after a lane drop, continues on a stretch with one lane in each direction, where the subject is left of the centre line with an oncoming vehicle closer than the required distance: the condition holds for part of the act only."}, {"name": "occasion_s3_outside", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The highway has one lane in each direction only before the act began; the whole pass is made after the road widens to two lanes in each direction."}, {"name": "occasion_s5", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "While the subject is left of the centre line, st.sight_distance at its point is above the subject's speed times p.passing_sight_time for the first part of the act and falls below it approaching a crest; no oncoming traffic."}, {"name": "occasion_s5_outside", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "st.sight_distance was below the bound before the act began and is above it at every observation of the act; no oncoming traffic."}, {"name": "occasion_s6", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Sight distance is ample; an oncoming road user of traffic comes within the required distance during the second half of the act while the subject is still left of the centre line."}, {"name": "occasion_s6_outside", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "An oncoming road user passed the subject before the act began; during the act no oncoming road user is within the required distance."}], "occasion": {"act": "drv.interaction.overtake_pass", "boundary": "window", "window": "p.overtake_window", "under_way": {"words": "overtaking and passing another vehicle proceeding in the same direction", "atoms": ["kin.velocity", "rel.bearing", "rel.longitudinal_overlap", "rel.same_direction"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"], "justification": "An observation inside the act lies after its beginning, the last observation of the window behind at which b was ahead of the subject with headings aligned (rel.bearing longitudinal component positive, rel.longitudinal_overlap negative, rel.same_direction), and at or before its recognition, while the subject's velocity (kin.velocity), exceeding b's along its heading, carries it up to and past b. These relations read the two road users' relative motion, never a place."}, "spans": {"s3": "some_moment", "s4": "at_recognition", "s5": "throughout", "s6": "throughout"}}, "literals": [{"span": "s3", "text": "two-lane", "value": 2, "unit": "count"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.overtake_window", "unit": "s", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the longest duration of an overtaking manoeuvre on an urban street, from having the overtaken vehicle ahead to having it behind", "source": "overtaking-manoeuvre durations in naturalistic driving studies"}, {"name": "p.overtake_same_direction_cos", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.9, "convention": "cosine of the largest heading difference (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as travelling in the same direction while one moves out to pass the other", "source": "lane-change heading angles in naturalistic driving data"}, {"name": "p.passing_sight_time", "unit": "s", "value": 11.0, "convention": "the MUTCD minimum passing sight distance (Table 3B-1, the warrant for a no-passing zone) divided by the prevailing speed it is tabulated for: about eleven seconds of travel across 25 to 70 mph; the sight distance or the clear distance a pass needs is the subject's speed times this time", "source": "MUTCD 2009 Section 3B.02, Table 3B-1"}, {"name": "p.oncoming_heading_cos", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.9, "convention": "cosine of the largest angle off exactly opposed headings (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as proceeding in opposite directions", "source": "heading geometry of two-way traffic"}, {"name": "p.conflict_horizon", "unit": "s", "value": 3.0, "convention": "time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash", "source": "traffic-conflict technique; FHWA Surrogate Safety Assessment Model"}, {"name": "p.conflict_centre_clearance", "unit": "m", "value": 3.0, "convention": "centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width", "source": "AASHTO passenger-car design-vehicle dimensions"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_213_2a", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-213-2a"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "A vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "must not be driven to the left side of the highway at any time:", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "When approaching the crest of a grade", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "or upon a curve in the highway", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "where the driver’s view is obstructed", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "within such distance as to create a hazard in the event another vehicle might approach from the opposite direction.", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "Subsection 2 does not apply upon a one-way highway.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'A vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["prim.region_lateral_offset", "st.centre_line", "st.on_way", "st.highway", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'the left side of the highway' is the side beyond its center (DEF-NRS-484A-040: 'to indicate each portion of a highway allocated to traffic proceeding in the two opposite directions, and, if a line is not marked, it is an imaginary line in the highway equally distant from the edges'): an st.centre_line c, 'the marking, or the geometric centre, dividing the two directions', lying (st.on_way) on the st.highway the subject occupies (rel.occupies), with prim.region_lateral_offset(subject, c) ('signed lateral offset (m, left positive)') negative: c lies to the right of the subject's reference point. 'at any time' places the duty at every observation. 'driven' is read through controlled motion (agency)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.crest", "st.region_geometry", "kin.position", "kin.velocity"], "derived": [], "justification": "'the crest of a grade' is st.crest, 'the place on a roadway's longitudinal profile where the slope changes from rising to falling in the direction of travel ... so the ground distance from a road user to it is read through st.region_geometry'; not st.grade, whose contract says it is 'Not a stand-in for: the place of a crest'. 'approaching' is the subject's velocity (kin.velocity) pointing toward the crest's reference point from its position (kin.position): the dot product of the velocity with the vector from the position to that point is positive; the crest is anchored to the subject by its ground distance (st.region_geometry), bounded in s6."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["st.curvature", "rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "'upon a curve in the highway': the subject occupies the st.highway (rel.occupies) and st.curvature, 'horizontal curvature of the roadway at a point, as a magnitude', at its point stands clear of zero by the source's resolution (p.curvature_resolution): a curve named without a size is its presence. Not kin.yaw_rate, which is 'Not a stand-in for: road curvature'."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["st.sight_distance"], "derived": [], "justification": "'the driver's view is obstructed': st.sight_distance at the subject's point, 'the distance along the road within which a vehicle at a point and another vehicle on the road could see each other ... whether or not any road user is there', short of the distance of s6. What the driver could see is read through the sight distance of the place (observable_reading, perception), not rel.visible, since the other vehicle is hypothetical."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.one_way_roadway"], "derived": [], "justification": "'upon a one-way highway': the subject occupies (rel.occupies) an st.one_way_roadway, 'roadway on which traffic is restricted to one direction'; there subsection 2 does not apply."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s6", "standard": "wi