": [], "justification": "'the crest of a grade' is st.crest, 'the place on a roadway's longitudinal profile where the slope changes from rising to falling in the direction of travel ... so the ground distance from a road user to it is read through st.region_geometry'; not st.grade, whose contract says it is 'Not a stand-in for: the place of a crest'. 'approaching' is the subject's velocity (kin.velocity) pointing toward the crest's reference point from its position (kin.position): the dot product of the velocity with the vector from the position to that point is positive; the crest is anchored to the subject by its ground distance (st.region_geometry), bounded in s6."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["st.curvature", "rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "'upon a curve in the highway': the subject occupies the st.highway (rel.occupies) and st.curvature, 'horizontal curvature of the roadway at a point, as a magnitude', at its point stands clear of zero by the source's resolution (p.curvature_resolution): a curve named without a size is its presence. Not kin.yaw_rate, which is 'Not a stand-in for: road curvature'."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["st.sight_distance"], "derived": [], "justification": "'the driver's view is obstructed': st.sight_distance at the subject's point, 'the distance along the road within which a vehicle at a point and another vehicle on the road could see each other ... whether or not any road user is there', short of the distance of s6. What the driver could see is read through the sight distance of the place (observable_reading, perception), not rel.visible, since the other vehicle is hypothetical."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.one_way_roadway"], "derived": [], "justification": "'upon a one-way highway': the subject occupies (rel.occupies) an st.one_way_roadway, 'roadway on which traffic is restricted to one direction'; there subsection 2 does not apply."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s6", "standard": "wi