point. 'driven' is read through controlled motion (agency)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.lane", "st.lane_adjacency", "st.on_way", "st.highway", "st.centre_line", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'two-directional highway' (DEF-NRS-484B-073) is 'an undivided highway upon which vehicles are allowed to proceed in opposite directions': the highway the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.highway) carries an st.centre_line, which divides 'the two directions of a two-way roadway', one roadway, so the way is undivided. 'two-lane': every st.lane lying on that highway (st.on_way) has an st.lane_adjacency 'count of the lanes in that direction' of a single lane, so the two directions carry the stated two lanes; the lane contract's exclusion ('lane ordinal equals roadway half only on a two-lane road') is met, the road being two-lane."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"], "justification": "'overtaking and passing another vehicle proceeding in the same direction' is drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, b): 'a, travelling in the same direction as b, comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it'; b is of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["st.sight_distance"], "derived": [], "justification": "'such left side is clearly visible': st.sight_distance at the subject's point, 'the distance along the road within which a vehicle at a point and another vehicle on the road could see each other ... whether or not any road user is there'; what a driver could see is read through that place's sight distance (observable_reading, perception), not rel.visible, since no actual road user need be there. Its extent is bounded by the standard of s7."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic", "rel.oncoming", "rel.centre_distance"], "derived": [], "justification": "'oncoming traffic': road users of the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic whose heading is opposed and closing to the subject's (rel.oncoming, 'headings opposed and closing'); 'free of' them for the distance of s7 is read on their rel.centre_distance to the subject, which is not used as a clearance between bodies but as the distance along the road ahead."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s7", "standard": "for a sufficient distance ahead to permit such overtaking and passing to be completely made without interfering with the safe operation of any vehicle approaching from the opposite direction or any vehicle overtaken", "concepts": ["st.sight_distance", "kin.speed", "rel.centre_distance", "rel.oncoming", "rel.contact", "prim.closest_approach_within", "prim.closest_approach_distance", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "params": ["p.passing_sight_time", "p.oncoming_heading_cos", "p.conflict_horizon", "p.conflict_centre_clearance"], "convention": "Passing sight distance: the MUTCD minimum passing sight distance by prevailing speed (Table 3B-1), expressed as the time the subject's speed takes to cover it (p.passing_sight_time), so the required distance moves with the subject's speed; both the sight distance at the subject's point and the centre distance to every oncoming road user of traffic must reach it. Interference with the safe operation of an oncoming vehicle or the vehicle overtaken: the traffic-conflict technique, a contact or a closest approach under constant velocities within p.conflict_horizon closer than p.conflict_centre_clearance.", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject, of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, overtakes and passes another road user b of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle: drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, b) with p.overtake_window and p.overtake_same_direction_cos is recognized at the judged observation; and at some observation of the act (from its beginning, the last observation of the window behind at which b was ahead with aligned headings, to its recognition) the subject occupies a highway h on which an st.centre_line c lies and every lane lying on h has a single lane in its direction (st.lane_adjacency count), the two-lane two-directional highway. b is quantified there, not a binder.", "obligation": "At every observation of the act at which the subject occupies such a highway h and prim.region_lateral_offset(subject, c) is negative for a centre line c lying on h (the subject on the left side of the center), all of the following hold; otherwise the duty is violated: st.sight_distance at the subject's point is at least the subject's kin.speed times p.passing_sight_time; every road user u of DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic with rel.oncoming(subject, u) under p.oncoming_heading_cos is at a rel.centre_distance of at least that same distance; and neither b nor any road user u of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle oncoming to the subject is in rel.contact with the subject, or has prim.closest_approach_within(subject, u) over p.conflict_horizon with prim.closest_approach_distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance.", "params": ["p.overtake_window", "p.overtake_same_direction_cos", "p.passing_sight_time", "p.oncoming_heading_cos", "p.conflict_horizon", "p.conflict_centre_clearance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s2", "why": "'driven to the left side of the center' is read as the subject's reference point lying beyond the centre line to its left; a body that only straddles the line with its reference point on the right is not read.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "'driven' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "'clearly visible' is read through the sight distance of the subject's place, what could be seen from it, not through any driver's perception.", "kind": "observable