sion_s6_outside", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "An oncoming road user passed the subject before the act began; during the act no oncoming road user is within the required distance."}], "occasion": {"act": "drv.interaction.overtake_pass", "boundary": "window", "window": "p.overtake_window", "under_way": {"words": "overtaking and passing another vehicle proceeding in the same direction", "atoms": ["kin.velocity", "rel.bearing", "rel.longitudinal_overlap", "rel.same_direction"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"], "justification": "An observation inside the act lies after its beginning, the last observation of the window behind at which b was ahead of the subject with headings aligned (rel.bearing longitudinal component positive, rel.longitudinal_overlap negative, rel.same_direction), and at or before its recognition, while the subject's velocity (kin.velocity), exceeding b's along its heading, carries it up to and past b. These relations read the two road users' relative motion, never a place."}, "spans": {"s5": "throughout", "s6": "throughout"}}, "literals": [{"span": "s2", "text": "two-lane", "value": 2, "unit": "count"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.overtake_window", "unit": "s", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the longest duration of an overtaking manoeuvre on an urban street, from having the overtaken vehicle ahead to having it behind", "source": "overtaking-manoeuvre durations in naturalistic driving studies"}, {"name": "p.overtake_same_direction_cos", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.9, "convention": "cosine of the largest heading difference (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as travelling in the same direction while one moves out to pass the other", "source": "lane-change heading angles in naturalistic driving data"}, {"name": "p.passing_sight_time", "unit": "s", "value": 11.0, "convention": "the MUTCD minimum passing sight distance (Table 3B-1, the warrant for a no-passing zone) divided by the prevailing speed it is tabulated for: 