_centre_clearance."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The subject passes b on b's right in the adjacent lane keeping its distance; no closest approach within p.conflict_horizon falls below p.conflict_centre_clearance and no contact occurs; no other road user is in the scene."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject follows b in the same lane at a steady gap and never passes it."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The subject draws past b on its right but rel.bearing is not observed: whether a pass on the right occurred is unknown.", "masked": ["rel.bearing"]}], "occasion": {"act": "drv.interaction.overtake_pass_on_right", "boundary": "window", "window": "p.overtake_window", "under_way": {"words": "overtake and pass another vehicle upon the right", "atoms": ["kin.velocity", "rel.bearing", "rel.longitudinal_overlap", "rel.same_direction"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.overtake_pass_on_right"], "justification": "An observation inside the act lies after its beginning, the last observation of the window behind at which b was ahead of the subject with headings aligned (rel.bearing longitudinal component positive, rel.longitudinal_overlap negative, rel.same_direction), and at or before its recognition, while the subject's velocity (kin.velocity), exceeding b's along its heading, carries it up to and past b. These relations are computed from the two road users' kinematics, so the boundary reads their relative motion, never a place."}, "spans": {}}, "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.overtake_window", "unit": "s", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the longest duration of an overtaking manoeuvre on an urban street, from having the overtaken vehicle ahead to having it behind", "source": "overtaking-manoeuvre durations in naturalistic driving studies"}, {"name": "p.overtake_same_direction_cos", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.9, "convention": "cosine of the largest heading difference (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as travelling in the same direction while one moves out to pass the other", "source": "lane-change heading angles in naturalistic driving data"}, {"name": "p.conflict_horizon", "unit": "s", "value": 3.0, "convention": "time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash", "source": "traffic-conflict technique; FHWA Surrogate Safety Assessment Model"}, {"name": "p.conflict_centre_clearance", "unit": "m", "value": 3.0, "convention": "centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width", "source": "AASHTO passenger-car design-vehicle dimensions"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_210_3", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-210-3"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "shall not overtake and pass another vehicle upon the right", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "when such movement requires driving off the paved portion of the highway.", "role": "condition"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole. 'driver' (DEF-NRS-484A-080) is a relational role read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading, agency)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.overtake_pass_on_right"], "justification": "'overtake and pass another vehicle upon the right' is the act drv.interaction.overtake_pass_on_right(subject, b), 'Road user a overtakes and passes road user b on b's right'; b is of DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.shoulder", "st.road_edge"], "derived": [], "justification": "'driving off the paved portion of the highway': at some observation of the act the subject's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies, 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region') an st.shoulder whose paved attribute is unset ('the part of the highway beside the roadway ...; paved attribute'), or an st.road_edge whose paved attribute, 'for the surface beyond it', is unset, so that part of the body is at or beyond the edge of the pavement. 'requires' is read through the movement as made (reading). 'highway' keeps its extent: the paved portion is any paved part of it, so a paved shoulder or sidewalk is not 'off' it."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subj