 the previous observation (rises). The trigger is read only where the subject occupies some lane (definedWhen): where it occupies none, the course change is unknown.", "obligation": "At that observation, for the side of the departure (left for heading_left_of_carrier, right for heading_right_of_carrier), the subject has shown sig.turn_indicator to that side or sig.hand_signal of meaning that side at every observation of the .path window of the subject's path behind it (holdsFor .path). The window is the stated 100 feet where asm.business_or_residence_district holds at that observation and the stated 300 feet where it does not (Term.cond); it is unknown where the assumption is undeclared or the window reaches before the recording. Otherwise the duty is violated.", "params": ["p.course_departure_sin_tol", "p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "The side of the signal is the side the heading departs to; a departure that later reverses is judged at its own onset.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "asm.business_or_residence_district false; the subject moves in its lane with sig.turn_indicator off and sig.hand_signal no_signal, then its heading turns left of the lane's direction beyond p.course_departure_sin_tol (a lane change to the left)."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "asm.business_or_residence_district false; the subject shows sig.turn_indicator left at every observation over the last stated 300 feet of its path before its heading departs to the left of its lane."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject keeps its heading along its lane's designated direction throughout; no course change begins."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The subject's heading departs to the right of its lane; neither sig.turn_indicator nor sig.hand_signal is observed on the source.", "masked": ["sig.turn_indicator", "sig.hand_signal"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "asm.business_or_residence_district true; the subject shows sig.turn_indicator right over a stretch of its path longer than the stated 100 feet but shorter than the stated 300 feet before its heading departs to the right of its lane."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "As branch_1 with asm.business_or_residence_district false: the indicator was not shown over the last stated 300 feet."}, {"name": "branch_3", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "asm.business_or_residence_district false; the subject shows sig.turn_indicator right over the last stated 300 feet and its heading departs to the left of its lane: the signal shows the wrong side."}], "literals": [{"span": "s1", "text": "100 feet", "value": 100, "unit": "ft"}, {"span": "s3", "text": "300 feet", "value": 300, "unit": "ft"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.course_departure_sin_tol", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.035, "convention": "sine of the largest angle (about two degrees) between a moving vehicle's heading and its lane's designated direction at which it counts as keeping its course: lane-keeping heading wander plus the source's heading noise, below the few degrees of heading a lane change takes", "source": "lane-keeping and lane-change heading-angle measurements in naturalistic driving data"}, {"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition source"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
